# New Repo Setup

RULE: Follow standard workflow for creating repos: GitHub CLI creation, team access (CosmicTrader, datado), scaffold, quality gates, workspace manifest, workspace venv install, dependency chain updates.
WHY: Consistent setup prevents missing steps (gitignore, venv, permissions, branch protection). Dependency chain ensures all repos can import new packages.
CODEX: 05-infrastructure/new-repo-setup.md

DO:
 gh repo create IggyIkenna/<repo> --private --clone
 gh api /repos/IggyIkenna/<repo>/collaborators/<user> -f permission='push'
 uv lock && uv pip install -e <repo>/ (from workspace root with venv active)
 Update workspace-manifest.json, dependent repos' pyproject.toml
 bash scripts/quickmerge.sh per repo

NEVER:
 Create repo without team access setup
 Skip workspace venv install (breaks imports in other repos)
 Skip uv lock after adding dependencies
 Forget to remove from .gitignore if previously ignored